From 0517c89956bbbdd06e943836765bd547c137e69f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:12:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: identify flat-file flush failure stages

Retain non-dropping Error severity, complete diagnostics and signed file
numbers for open/truncate/commit failures. Existing SourceFunction metadata
retains __func__ with no eager string formatting or new registry keys.
All file operations, close/return ordering and failure behavior stay intact.

Add one actual open-failure case using a directory at an owned temporary
file path. Flush returns false, the directory stays empty, and JSON has
the exact old message/function/file number. Existing normal flush cases
remain. Truncate/commit failures are not newly forced or claimed tested.

Shared eCash flat-file owner. Source-only event lint/diff checks pass;
new native case NOT_COMPILED/NOT_RUN. Sealed381/current intake unchanged.

Scripted production diff:
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --root . --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/flatfile-flush-failures.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/flatfile406-conversion.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/flatfile.cpp src/test/flatfile_tests.cpp

Source validation:
